delinquency_roster.json: pulled once on 12 Oct 2026 from the public FDIC BankFind API (https://banks.data.fdic.gov/api/financials, one request, filters CERT:(the 16 certs in config/peers.json) AND REPDTE:[20170331 TO 20260630], fields CERT, REPDTE and the 20 fields of peers/delinquency.FIELDS); 608 rows, 16 banks x 38 quarters 2017Q1-2026Q2, the API's meta total matched, no blank values; kept as {YYYYMMDD: [rows]} like roster_2006.json, one row per bank per quarter, only those fields, sorted by CERT. The pull script was a throwaway and is not kept.
These are the API's values, not the filing's: nothing in this fixture or its tests has been tied to KeyBank's RC-N on the FFIEC CDR (V1-ROUND2-SPEC acceptance item 2 is that check, made separately).

14 Oct 2026: LNCONRP (RC-C 6.b, other revolving credit plans) added to roster_2006.json, roster_1992.json and delinquency_roster.json, one request each to https://api.fdic.gov/banks/financials (filters CERT:(the 16 certs) AND REPDTE:[first TO last], fields CERT, REPDTE, LNCONRP); every row matched, the API's meta totals 1,312, 2,155 and 608. It is blank in every quarter before 2001: the FDIC data has no 6.b until 2001Q1. Other consumer's balance is now 6.b + 6.d; the acceptance tests reproduce the 6 Oct build on a copy with 6.b at 0 (conftest.as_earlier_build), since that build divided by 6.d alone. The script was a throwaway and is not kept.

14 Oct 2026, later: RSSDHCR (each filer's top holding company) added to the same three fixtures the same way (meta totals 1,312, 2,155 and 608), because 'peers build' now requires it (books.restarted reads it on every flow). It is blank for Zions (2270) from 2018Q3, after its holding company merged into the bank: 32 rows in each fixture, a fact, not a gap.
peers_workbook_642ff55f.py: src/threshold_engine/peers/peers_workbook.py copied unchanged from commit 642ff55f (branch threshold-engine-book, 14 Oct 2026), the last version with one tab per view (Pack, Peers, Delinquency, Balances, Lagged, Normalisation, Mix). tests/test_peers_dashboard.py loads it beside today's module and requires every view on the Peers dashboard to equal the old builder's value for the same quantity with every bank switched on (and, until 15 Oct 2026, tests/test_peers_into.py required the series CSVs both builds write to be the same byte for byte). It is code under test, not data.
Retired 14 Oct 2026: peers_workbook_d1e353a1.py, which pinned the standalone workbook part for part as it was before the into/names option. The standalone output was changed on purpose (the one-tab dashboard), so that comparison and the copy were retired together, as that note said they would be.
peers_workbook_96ee5f2f.py: src/threshold_engine/peers/peers_workbook.py copied unchanged from commit 96ee5f2f (14 Oct 2026), the first one-tab dashboard, before Claude Design's round 2 layout. tests/test_peers_into.py requires the series CSVs both builds write to be the same byte for byte. It is code under test, not data.
