commercial_2007.json (16 Oct 2026): five filers, 2006Q3 to 2008Q2 (40 rows), every commercial field of peers/books.COMMERCIAL and peers/delinquency.FIELDS plus RSSDHCR, kept as {YYYYMMDD: [rows]} sorted by CERT, values exactly as they are in the cache `peers pull` wrote that day (https://api.fdic.gov/banks/financials, index risview_20260819185831, one request per quarter, every filer; nulls kept as null). The five: KeyBank (17534) and JPMorgan (628), CALLFORM 31; Sovereign Bank (29950), CALLFORM 100 (the TFR), which never filed the nonfarm split; Bank of China (33653), CALLFORM 2, which files a C&I balance and no charge-off, past-due or nonaccrual field; Graystone Bank (58166), CALLFORM 41, which filed the nonfarm split as 0 and 0 through 2007 and filed it from 2008Q1. The call forms were read from the same API on 16 Oct 2026 (field CALLFORM, 2007Q1). KeyBank's 2007Q1 split (4,278,597 + 4,495,612 = 8,774,209) matches docs/commercial-2026-10/research-fdic.md (on main). The selection script was a throwaway and is not kept.

keybank_ci_2005.json (17 Oct 2026): KeyBank (17534) alone, 2005Q1 to 2026Q2 (86 rows), the fields CERT, REPDTE, LNCI, DRCI, CRCI, P3CI, P9CI, NACI and RSSDHCR, kept as {YYYYMMDD: [row]}, values exactly as they are in the commercial cache `peers pull` wrote on 16 Oct 2026 from https://api.fdic.gov/banks/financials (one request per quarter, every filer; LOG.md, 16 Oct 2026, the commercial data layer). Its C&I balance falls from 41,865,646 at 2024Q3 to 29,882,121 at 2024Q4 (-28.6%), the move docs/commercial-2026-10/research-breaks.md (on main) records as the NDFI and margin-loan revision (41.9 to 29.9, $bn). tests/test_reporting_changes.py reads it for the firm's answer to the commercial proposal's question 15 (its C&I rose 18.0% in 2020Q1, under the 25% jump). tests/test_left_out.py reads it for question 16 (the 2024Q4 move, which the registry names for C&I). The selection script was a throwaway and is not kept.

keybank_ci_1991.json (18 Oct 2026): KeyBank (17534) and the four banks the FDIC history record says it absorbed in 1992 and 1993 (6568 in 1992Q1; 746 and 26650 in 1992Q3; 777 in 1993Q3), 1991Q1 to 1993Q4, 38 rows (a bank has no row after it was absorbed), the fields CERT, REPDTE, LNCI, DRCI, CRCI, P3CI, P9CI, NACI and RSSDHCR, kept as {YYYYMMDD: [rows]} sorted by CERT, values exactly as they are in the commercial cache `peers pull` wrote on 16 Oct 2026 (https://api.fdic.gov/banks/financials, one request per quarter, every filer; nulls kept as null). P3CI (30-89 days) is null in every row: the FDIC data has it from 2001Q1. tests/test_from_1991.py reads it for the firm's answer to the commercial proposal's question 6 (history from 1991Q1). The selection script was a throwaway and is not kept.

history_1990.json (18 Oct 2026): twelve FDIC history rows, exactly as https://api.fdic.gov/banks/history returned them on 18 Oct 2026 to fdic.history("1990-01-01") (filters EFFDATE:[1990-01-01 TO *] AND ACQ_CERT:[1 TO *], fields fdic.FIELDS plus ID; 35,742 rows in all that day): the three code 213 rows (May 1990), the one code 225 row (9 Oct 1991), and KeyBank's four absorptions of 1992 and 1993 (codes 222 and 223) with the 810 mirror row of each. The full pull that day, classified, matched the cache's mergers-since-1990.json and absorptions-since-1990.json exactly (5,946 acquirers, 16,362 absorptions). tests/test_from_1991.py reads it. The selection script was a throwaway and is not kept.
